  "pli-tv-bu-vb-pc36:2.1.10": "As with the previous rule, the punctuation of the Pali is wrong. An additional comma is required between <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ṭhito</i> and <i lang='pi' translate='no'>abhiharati</i>. “They” refers to the donor, whether male or female. ",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-pc36:2.1.11": "",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-pc36:2.1.12": "Literally, “It is done with what is not allowable.” ",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-pc36:2.1.13": "The “it”, both here and below, refers to the ceremony of making it left over. ",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-pc36:2.1.14": "Literally, “It is not done lifted.” ",
